      "url": "https://www.maastrichtuniversity.nl/",
      "title": "The European university of the Netherlands | Maastricht University",
      "text": "Skip to main content\nNederlands\nMy UM\nEducation\nOpen Education\nResearch\nOpen Research\nAbout UM\nOpen About UM\nNews & events\nOpen News & events\nSearch on the website\nThe European university of the Netherlands\nOur education\nOur research\nAt the heart of Europe, across borders, across disciplines. Here we work together on a better tomorrow.\nAbout Maastricht University\nVisit our Bachelor’s Open Day!\nWorking at Maastricht University\nCalendar\nMore events\n2\nNov\n5\nNov\nAll about our master's programmes!\nOnline Master's Week\n14\nNov\nGet a taste of the atmosphere!\nBachelor's Open Day\n19\nNov\nStudium Generale | Tans Lecture\nThe Case Against Conscious AI\nCelebrate UM50 with us\n50 years of Maastricht University\nVisit the UM50 website\n \nFrom trash to treasure: join UM50's Doorspace x Circular Engineering workshops\n \nUM student Juraj Vitek lives in the modern student complex StuNest: “I enjoy co…\n \nPlastic Recycling Heroes: little heroes, big impact\nNews and stories\nMore news and stories\nThreads Completed: The Tapestry of Limburg’s History of Slavery\n29 October 2026\nIn 2025, historians Diana Miryong Natermann and Christian Ernsten launched a research project on the history of slavery in the province of Limburg. The research was translated into a design for a 35-meter-long tapestry.\nEvent series 'The Perfect Storm' offers new perspectives on global unrest\n29 October 2026\nMany people in the Netherlands are worried and feel uncertain about the future. For them, the event series The Perfect Storm, organised by our Platform for Outreach and Co-Creation, is well worth attending, says coordinator Mariëlle Wijermars.\n“The starting point for integrated neighbourhood care is the story of the neighbourhood”\n28 October 2026\nCreating a healthy and vibrant neighbourhood is a joint effort. But how can professionals and residents work together effectively? Arianne Elissen and Anne van den Bulck explored this in the LIME project ‘Working together for healthy neighbourhoods’.\nFour Vidi grants for talented Maastricht University researchers\n22 October 2026\nThe Netherlands Organisation for Scientific Research (NWO) has awarded four experienced researchers from UM Vidi funding, totalling 850,000 euros. This will enable them to develop their own innovative line of research and set up a research group.\nUM websites and systems accessible again following security update\n21 October 2026\nThe UM has carried out security updates on its main websites and systems in response to vulnerabilities in the PHP programming language, which is used across large parts of the internet. Most of the platforms are accessible again.\nWhy don’t suspects talk? “We’re quick to think: they must be guilty”\n14 October 2026\nLegal researchers Dr Melanie Sauerland and Professor Miet Vanderhallen study why suspects exercise their right to remain silent — and what consequences this may have.\nGo to previous slide\nGo to next slide\nDirectly to\nFaculties\nResearch institutes\nPress\nFind your way in Maastricht\nStudent support\nAdmission and enrolment\nUM visiting address\nMinderbroedersberg 4-6\n6211 LK Maastricht\n+31 43 388 2222\nUM postal address\nP.O. Box 616\n6200 MD Maastricht\nSocial media\nBluesky\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nTikTok\nYouTube\nMenu footer (EN)\nContact\nTransparency & Accountability\nPrivacy & security\nSupport\nFeedback",
